  "worked_solution": "The set of all points $(x,y)$ that are a distance of $25$ units from the origin defines a circle with radius $r=25$ centered at the origin, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/d526d47989c735bcdd8629b76246c3bd88d4b3a142bcdffb33ea8bc0c51cb31e.png)\n\nSo, the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={25}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =625.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
